    "note": "Introduced version. Section 9 repeals the permit-required offence (subd. 1a), permit display duty (subd. 1b), out-of-state permit recognition (subd. 16) and section 624.7181 (rifles and shotguns in public places). Sections 3-7 conform the permit text to \"optional\". Subd. 1c(a) states a legislative finding on the second amendment; not a duty on the state."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 1c): (b) A person who is not prohibited from possessing a firearm by any law of this state or any federal law shall have the right to carry, hold, or possess a firearm in a motor vehicle, snowmobile, or boat, or on or about the person's clothes or the person, or otherwise in possession or control in a public place.\nSection 2 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 1d): A person may apply for an optional permit to carry a pistol as provided in this section.\nSection 8 (Minn. Stat. 624.714, subd. 23): No sheriff, police chief, governmental unit, government official, government employee, or other person or body acting under color of law or governmental authority may change, modify, or supplement these criteria or procedures, or limit the exercise of the right to carry a firearm."
}